  "rationale": "The workflow is a tag-triggered release workflow with a single job that only checks out code, reads the latest tag, generates a changelog, and creates a GitHub release. It has no dependency installation, build, or test steps, so the dependency-cache pattern (P-LIT-GHA-CACHE) has nothing to cache. The custom-timeout pattern (P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT) lacks representative successful-duration history (CI history shows no completed runs), so an informed timeout budget cannot be chosen. Cancel-stale (P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE) is contraindicated because this is release/deployment work. No other evidence-supported pattern fits this workflow without making unrelated changes.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT", "P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE"]
}
